{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.QuantumVolume","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.QuantumVolume","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.quantumVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.quantumVolume","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-volume.lean#L74-L79","doc":"**Quantum volume** of a region with |U| brane points (homogeneous gas).\nV_q(U) = |U| · Vol(S³_q).\nLabel: def:quantum-volume ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:quantum-volume","label":"def:quantum-volume","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-volume.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.s3FibreVolume_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.s3FibreVolume_classical","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-volume.lean#L67-L72","doc":"At classicality (q = 1), Vol(S³_q) = 2π² = Vol(S³). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.s3FibreVolume_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.s3FibreVolume_pos","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-volume.lean#L57-L65","doc":"The S³ fibre volume is positive when q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.s3FibreVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.s3FibreVolume","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-volume.lean#L50-L55","doc":"**S³ fibre volume** in the q-deformed metric.\nVol(S³_q) = π² · [2]_q = π²(q + q⁻¹).\nLabel: def:quantum-volume ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qInteger_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qInteger_two","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-volume.lean#L30-L48","doc":"[2]_q = q + q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qInteger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qInteger","kind":"def","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-volume.lean#L21-L28","doc":"The q-integer [n]_q = (q^n - q^{-n}) / (q - q^{-1}). ","signatureChunk":0}]}